# Claude
CLAUDE.user.md

# Brigade
# Committed research evidence must never be swallowed by the seeded Node template's broad patterns
# (`logs`, `out`, `dist` and `*.out` match at any depth).
!docs/research/**

# Build output, local environment files and Supabase CLI state (plan 7.6). `/bin/` is anchored at the repo root on
# purpose: `plugin/bin/` is committed. `dist-cross` is NOT matched by the template's bare `dist`, hence its own line.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/bin/
/dist/
/dist-cross/
cover.out
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.env

# Compiled Python from the promoted Phase 0 experiment drivers. 25 .pyc files were swept into the index by the
# canonical `git add --verbose :/ .` chain (the `commit` target's stage step) before this rule existed; they have
# since been removed from the index (`git rm --cached`) and stay on disk, because the drivers still run.
# scripts/ci/fixtures_test.go fails `make test` if one is ever tracked again.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Belt and braces for the same hazard (plan 7.6). `logs`, `out`, `dist` and `*.out` match at ANY depth, and the
# `.env.*` / `cover.out` lines above match by basename at any depth too, so the research negations are restated
# here, LAST, where nothing appended above can override them. Invariant: `git status --ignored docs/research`
# must list nothing, and `git ls-files -i -c --exclude-standard` must be empty.
!docs/research/**/logs/
!docs/research/**/logs/**
!docs/research/**/out/
!docs/research/**/out/**
!docs/research/**/dist/
!docs/research/**/dist/**
!docs/research/**/*.out
!docs/research/**

# macOS: the canonical commit chain is `git add --verbose :/ .` (the user's gcp script), so one Finder
# visit to any directory would otherwise commit a binary dropping. The seeded go,node template has no
# macOS section and plan 7.6 does not add one.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Local AI-tooling state, same hazard as the .pyc rule above: the canonical `git add --verbose :/ .` chain
# swept these into a commit on 2026-09-09 (e33690e) before this rule existed; removed with `git rm --cached`,
# left on disk since Claude Code and the Serena MCP server both still use them locally.
.claude/.claude-md-seen-mtimes
.serena/
